{"description":"Enforce per-role guardrails with REAL containment: per-worker scratch HOME (the host HOME is dropped from the worker env allow-list), OS-level FS confinement on Linux (landlock, or a distinct UID owning `~/.eka` at 0700), macOS `sandbox-exec`, Windows deferred-and-documented; per-worker git worktree (stated as VCS isolation, NOT a security boundary); a default-deny ACP permission policy with timeout=\u003edeny. Guardrails are code-owned and non-optional in v1. Secrets are injected per-driver via the secrets broker, never from `os.Environ()`.","acceptanceCriteria":"Workers run with the allow-listed env only (no host HOME, no secret tokens); a worker cannot read `~/.eka` or host credential dotfiles (negative tests).\nEach worker gets its own git worktree; the worktree is documented as VCS isolation, not a security boundary.\nACP permission requests are default-denied, timed out to deny, and never hang.\nDrivers are pinned (exact version + checksum); an unknown/unpinned driver is refused.\nThe containment is enabled by default with no opt-out in v1."}